{"authored" [{"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{t+8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=\\pi ?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(\\pi )=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "f945047955e33b6065b36bf5537f6934c9065f79a354f7c7f7118ad50c801644" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\pi $ into our function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(\\pi ) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi +8} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\pi +1) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "f945047955e33b6065b36bf5537f6934c9065f79a354f7c7f7118ad50c801644" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha